tooling/spark/prompts/invert-assumption.md: Problem:

{{problem}}

First, list the assumptions...

prompts.raw:
Problem:

{{problem}}

The usual solutions operate on this problem's core objects in their default representation. Re-express the core object in a fundamentally different representation — a different coordinate system, basis, transform, encoding, or structure. Identify precisely what the new representation makes cheap or trivial that the default made hard, and propose the solution that exploits that. A few sentences.

prompts.label:
tooling/spark/prompts/representation-shift.md: Problem:

{{problem}}

The usual solutions operate...

prompts.raw:
Problem:

{{problem}}

Pick a domain far from this problem (e.g. biology, logistics, music, geology, finance, ecology). Map this problem's structure onto that domain. Find a technique that is standard there, and translate it back. Propose the solution this analogy suggests, even if unconventional. Name the domain and the borrowed technique. A few sentences.

