tooling/spark/prompts/analogy-collision.md: Problem:

{{problem}}

Pick a domain far from this...

prompts.raw:
Problem:

{{problem}}

Do not solve it yet. First write 6 sharp questions about it that nobody usually asks — questions that challenge why it is framed this way at all. Then pick the single most generative question and pursue it into a concrete approach. Propose that approach. A few sentences after the questions.

prompts.label:
tooling/spark/prompts/self-question.md: Problem:

{{problem}}

Do not solve it yet. First ...

prompts.raw:
Problem:

{{problem}}

Identify the one constraint everyone treats as non-negotiable (e.g. exactness, completeness, determinism, fixed order, full precision). Drop it entirely. With it gone, what fundamentally different STRUCTURE or representation becomes available that the constraint used to forbid? Build the solution around that new structure — not the textbook relaxation everyone reaches for — then state the condition under which it stays valid for the original problem. A few sentences.

